// The serializer records where the decompiler placed each return value
// (`return_storage`) and parameter (`parameter_storage`).  When the return
// storage holds more bytes than the declared return type, the lifted function
// cannot return the upper part: a 64-bit value in r0:r1 declared as a 32-bit
// int loses r1.  That is reported as a warning, and as an error under -strict.
// Storage that fits, void storage, and a prototype with no storage recorded
// (JSON from an older serializer) are not reported.
//
// RUN: bash %strip-json-comments %s > %t.json
// RUN: %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-cir -print-tu -output %t > %t.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=WARN %s --input-file %t.log
// RUN: test -e %t.cir
// RUN: not %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-cir -strict -output %t.strict > %t.strict.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=ERR %s --input-file %t.strict.log
// RUN: test ! -e %t.strict.cir
//
// WARN: Diag Warning: {{.*}}lossy lift [return-narrowed]: function 'ret_pair_as_int' returns 8 bytes in r1, r0 but its declared return type 'unsigned int' holds 4 bytes
// WARN-NOT: Diag Error
// WARN-NOT: function 'ret_pair_as_u64'
// WARN-NOT: function 'ret_single'
// WARN-NOT: function 'ret_void'
// WARN-NOT: function 'ret_no_storage'
//
// ERR: Diag Error: {{.*}}lossy lift [return-narrowed]: function 'ret_pair_as_int' returns 8 bytes in r1, r0
